{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he shall break it, etc., a flagon (נבל).</b> A vessel of a potter." "<b>Shall not spare.</b> To break it." "<b>To take fire.</b> Like יחתה (Proverbs 6:27), גחלים אתה חותה על ראשו (Proverbs 25:22), and it is of doubled-root verbs." "<b>And to uncover.</b> From the derivation of מחשוף הלבן (Genesis 30:37); חשף יי את זרוע קדשו (Isaiah 52:10)." "<b>From a cistern (מגבא).</b> From the derivation of וגבאיו (Ezekiel 47:11); he translated it as 'pit' in Aramaic. And the meaning of לחשוף is 'to uncover,' for the waters are hidden, and this is the meaning concerning those who go down to Egypt."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:01.336450724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}